% Description: Yukon non-linear optimisation -- Vary two variables, Minimize a quadratic cost, and apply a NonlinearConstraint inside an Optimize block (no spacecraft / propagation, purely algebraic).

Create Yukon Yukon1
Yukon1.ShowProgress          = true
Yukon1.ReportStyle           = Normal
Yukon1.MaximumIterations     = 500
Yukon1.UseCentralDifferences = false
Yukon1.FeasibilityTolerance  = 0.001
Yukon1.HessianUpdateMethod   = SelfScaledBFGS
Yukon1.MaximumFunctionEvals  = 1000
Yukon1.OptimalityTolerance   = 0.0001
Yukon1.FunctionTolerance     = 0.0001
Yukon1.MaximumElasticWeight  = 10000

Create ReportFile Data
Data.Filename     = 'yukon_optimization.report'
Data.Precision    = 16
Data.WriteHeaders = false
Data.LeftJustify  = On
Data.ZeroFill     = Off
Data.FixedWidth   = true
Data.Delimiter    = ' '
Data.ColumnWidth  = 20
Data.WriteReport  = true
Data.Add          = {X1, X2}

Create Variable X1 X2 J G

BeginMissionSequence

Optimize Yukon1 {SolveMode = Solve, ExitMode = DiscardAndContinue}

   Vary 'Vary X1' Yukon1(X1 = 0, {Perturbation = 0.0000001, MaxStep = 9.999999e300})
   Vary 'Vary X2' Yukon1(X2 = 0, {Perturbation = 0.0000001, MaxStep = 9.999999e300})

   'Compute Cost (J)' J = ( X1 - 2 )^2 + ( X2 - 2 )^2
   Minimize 'Minimize Cost J' Yukon1(J)

   'Compute Constraint (G)' G = X2 + X1
   NonlinearConstraint 'G = 8' Yukon1(G<=8)
   Report Data X1 X2

EndOptimize
